    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Southern Company Services receives up-front payments for studies and operating companies do not record any charges to these accounts. Costs are bore at system level. The only time an operating company would have anything to report on page 231 is when the charges exceed the amount collected and the customer does not reimburse Southern Company. Any study completed by an operating company and is under the OATT should be reported by that operating company on page 231.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Southern Company Services receives up-front payments for studies and operating companies do not record any charges to these accounts. Costs are bore at system level. The only time an operating company would have anything to report on page 231 is when the charges exceed the amount collected and the customer does not reimburse Southern Company. Any study completed by an operating company and is under the OATT should be reported by that operating company on page 231.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Earned vacation pay is deferred and recognized only when paid as ordered by the Georgia Public Service Commission (PSC) in Docket No. 3270.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">In accordance with the Plant Vogtle Units 3 and 4 Prudency Stipulation in Docket No. 29849, and as a result of Plant Vogtle Unit 4 being placed in service on April 29, 2024, the unprotected deficient accumulated deferred income taxes associated with the remeasurement of deferred income taxes on the construction work in progress for Plant Vogtle Units 3 and 4 as a result of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act will be recovered over a period of 10 years starting in May 2024. In accordance with certain provisions of the Inflation Reduction Act, the Company has elected to opt out of normalization requirements on certain federal investment tax credits (ITC) and has amortized the ITC more rapidly than over the asset life.</span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"></span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">The ITCs that have been amortized more rapidly than over the underlying asset lives will be classified as regulatory assets, FERC 182, and will offset the unamortized ITC balances in FERC account 255, Deferred ITC in accordance with ASC 980 overlay accounting.</span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"></span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">The amortization of the ITC Normalization Opt-out balances in FERC account 182 will offset the amortization of the unamortized ITC balances from FERC 255 over the asset lives.</span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"></span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">The remaining deferred income taxes are being amortized over the related remaining property lives in accordance with IRS normalization principles which may range up to 58 years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Retiree benefit plans are recovered through current rates over the average remaining service period as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 4565, which may range up to 14 years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Nuclear outage costs are deferred and amortized over the respective unit&#8217;s operating cycle as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 4007.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Coal Combustion Residuals (CCR) AROs are recovered through the Environmental Compliance Cost Recovery tariff, with approximately $160 million, $100 million, and $220 million recovered in 2023, 2024, and 2025, respectively, and approximately $220 million expected to be recovered annually from 2026 through 2028.</span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"></span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Effective January 1, 2023, approximately $17 million annually is being recovered for non-CCR AROs in traditional base tariffs through December 31, 2028. Other cost of removal obligations and non-CCR AROs are recovered over the related property lives, which may range up to 58 years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Realized and unrealized losses arising from marked to market gas and electric hedges are deferred and recovered when settled as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 16134. The Company's natural gas hedging program uses an array of derivative instruments within a 36-month time horizon, as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 43011.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Effective January 1, 2023, the Company is accruing $31 million annually through December 31, 2025, as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280, to cover the operations and maintenance costs of damages from major storms to its transmission and distribution facilities, which are recoverable through base rates. Based on the Alternate Rate Plan Extension Stipulation approved by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280, the Company filed for a rate adjustment in 2026 related to the under-recovered storm costs incurred through December 31, 2025. A decision by the Georgia PSC is expected in May 2026.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Effective January 1, 2023, the Company is accruing $5 million annually through December 31, 2028, as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280, to cover the costs of environmental remediation.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">In accordance with the Georgia PSC orders in Docket Nos. 34218, 36498, 42310 and 44160, deferred plant retirement costs, including remaining net book values and unusable materials and supplies inventories, are classified as a regulatory asset. The remaining net book values of Plant Hammond Units 3 and 4 are being amortized over a period equal to the units' remaining useful lives as approved by the Georgia PSC in Docket Nos. 31958 and 36989, respectively. Effective January 1, 2023, the remaining net book value of Plants Wansley Units 1 and 2 is being amortized over a period equal to the units' remaining useful lives as approved by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 42516 and the remaining net book value of Plant Wansley CT Unit 5A was amortized over a three-year period ending December 31, 2025, as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280. Effective January 1, 2026, the remaining net book values of Plant Hammond Unit 4 and Plant Wansley Units 1 and 2 will be amortized over a 13-year period ending December 31, 2038 based on the ARP Extension Stipulation approved by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280. The decision on the timing of the recovery of the unusable materials and supplies inventories will be deferred until a future base rate case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Effective January 1, 2023, certain implementation costs related to software and cloud computing projects incurred through 2022 were deferred and are being amortized over a five-year period ending December 31, 2027, in accordance with the Georgia PSC order in Docket No. 44280. The recovery of deferred costs incurred since 2022 will be determined by the Georgia PSC in the next base rate case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">In accordance with the Georgia PSC order in Docket Nos. 42310 and 42311, the costs of energy efficient upgrades, prepaid by the Company, for participating customers associated with the Income Qualified Tariff Based Energy Efficiency Pilot, or Residential Investment Saving Energy Pilot, are deferred and recovered from those customers over the life of the installed equipment not to exceed ten years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">In accordance with the Nuclear Regulatory Commission requirement to satisfy funding assurance for nuclear decommissioning, the Company provided funding to the external nuclear decommissioning trust for Plant Vogtle Units 1, 3, and 4 in the amounts of $0.8 million, $7.6 million, and $7.8 million, respectively, in 2023, $0.4 million, $7.6 million, and $7.8 million, respectively, in 2024, and for Plant Vogtle Units 3 and 4 of $7.6 million and $7.8 million, respectively, in 2025. Effective August 1, 2023, the Company is amortizing $7.6 million annually until the next base rate case, as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 43838, for the funding of future costs related to decommissioning Plant Vogtle Unit 3. As ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 29849, and as a result of Plant Vogtle Unit 4 being placed in service on April 29, 2024, the Company is amortizing $7.8 million annually effective May 1, 2024 until the next base rate case, for the funding of future costs related to decommissioning Plant Vogtle Unit 4. The recovery of the funding for Plant Vogtle Unit 1 will be determined by the Georgia PSC in the next base rate case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">In accordance with the Plant Vogtle Unit 3 Base Rate Filing Order in Docket No. 43838, financing costs on Plant Vogtle Unit 3 and common facilities capital and construction costs above $2.1 billion and excluded from the Nuclear Construction Cost Recovery Tariff were deferred to a regulatory asset until Plant Vogtle Unit 4 achieved commercial operation. In accordance with the Plant Vogtle Units 3 and 4 Prudency Stipulation in Docket No. 29849, and as a result of Plant Vogtle Unit 4 being placed in service on April 29, 2024, the Company is amortizing these financing costs effective May 1, 2024 over a 10-year period ending April 30, 2034.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In accordance with the Georgia PSC order in Docket No. 44280 to recover the net book values of Plants Bowen and Scherer through 2034, $40 million and $70 million of the depreciation for Plants Bowen and Scherer, respectively, are being deferred annually to a regulatory asset over the units' remaining useful lives through 2030 and 2028, respectively. Subsequently, based on the Alternate Rate Plan Extension Stipulation approved by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280, effective January 1, 2026, the depreciable lives of Plants Bowen and Scherer will be extended to 2038 and the Company will no longer defer any depreciation expense for Plants Bowen and Scherer and amortize the deferred depreciation regulatory asset balance as of December 31, 2025 over a 13-year period ending December 31, 2038. In accordance with the Plant Vogtle Unit 3 Base Rate Filing Order in Docket No. 43838, depreciation on Vogtle Unit 3 and common facilities capital and construction costs above $2.1 billion were deferred to a regulatory asset until Vogtle Unit 4 achieved commercial operation. In accordance with the Vogtle Units 3 and 4 Prudency Stipulation in Docket No. 29849, the Company is amortizing the regulatory asset balance effective May 1, 2024 over a 10-year period ending April 30, 2034.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In accordance with the Georgia PSC order in Docket No. 29849, the under-recovered amount associated with the Nuclear Construction Cost Recovery Tariff was deferred to a regulatory asset and the recovery of the under-recovered amount will be determined by the Georgia PSC in the next base rate case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In accordance with the 2022 ARP Extension Stipulation in Docket No. 44280, certain regulatory liabilities, which were fully amortized as of December 31, 2025, will continue to be amortized over the 2022 ARP extension period, resulting in a regulatory asset. Future recovery will be determined in the next base rate base.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">The protected excess accumulated deferred income taxes (ADITs) associated with the remeasurement of ADITS as a result of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act are amortized over the related remaining property lives using the average rate assumption method in accordance with IRS normalization principles which may range up to 58 years. In 2025, the Company deferred approximately $255 million of IRC section 45U nuclear tax credits related to the 2024 tax year in accordance with the 2022 Alternate Rate Plan, which directed the Company to defer any new tax credits from the Inflation Reduction Act that were generated during the 2023-2025 ARP period as approved by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280.</span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"></span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Based on the Alternate Rate Plan Extension Stipulation approved by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280 in July 2025, these regulatory liability balances will be amortized over a 3-year period ending December 31, 2028. The deferred tax assets and regulatory liabilities associated with the remaining unamortized investment tax credits are being amortized over the related remaining property lives in accordance with IRS normalization principles which may range up to approximately 41 years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">In April 2025, the State of Georgia enacted tax legislation that reduced the corporate income tax rate from 5.39% to 5.19% effective for the 2025 tax year. The legislation triggered a remeasurement, in the second quarter of 2025, of the Company&#8217;s existing ADIT balances by approximately $39 million that was recorded as a regulatory liability.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Effective January 1, 2023, no funding will be accrued for the Plant Hatch Units 1 and 2 and Plant Vogtle Units 1 and 2 external nuclear decommissioning trusts until the next base rate case as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280. Effective August 1, 2023, the Company is accruing $7.6 million annually until the next base rate case, as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 43838, for the funding of future costs related to decommissioning Plant Vogtle Unit 3. As ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 29849, and as a result of Plant Vogtle Unit 4 being placed in service on April 29, 2024, the Company is accruing $7.8 million annually effective May 1, 2024 until the next base rate case, for the funding of future costs related to decommissioning Plant Vogtle Unit 4.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Coal Combustion Residuals (CCR) AROs are recovered through the Environmental Compliance Cost Recovery tariff, with approximately $160 million, $100 million, and $220 million recovered in 2023, 2024, and 2025, respectively, and approximately $220 million expected to be recovered annually from 2026 through 2028. Effective January 1, 2023, approximately $17 million annually is being recovered for non-CCR AROs through traditional base tariffs through December 31, 2028. Other cost of removal obligations and non-CCR AROs are recovered over the related property lives, which may range up to 58 years.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Realized and unrealized gains arising from marked to market gas and electric hedges are deferred and recovered when settled as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 16134. The Company's natural gas hedging program uses an array of derivative instruments within a 36-month time horizon, as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 43011.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">The costs associated with Demand-Side Management (DSM) initiatives are recovered through the DSM tariffs, and the revenues and expenses are trued-up based on actual results. Based on the Alternate Rate Plan Extension Stipulation approved by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 44280 in July 2025, the DSM tariffs will not be adjusted until the next base rate case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">The credits associated with retiree benefit plans resulted from a change in valuation methodology and are being amortized over 13 years ending December 31, 2032.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In accordance with the Georgia PSC order in Docket No. 44280, the credit balance of the remaining net book values of Plant Boulevard Unit 1, Plant McIntosh Unit 1, and Plant Langdale Units 5 and 6 as of December 31, 2022 was amortized over a three-year period ending December 31, 2025.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In accordance with the Nuclear Regulatory Commission requirement to satisfy funding assurance for nuclear decommissioning, the Company provided funding to the external nuclear decommissioning trust for Plant Vogtle Units 1, 3, and 4 in the amounts of $0.8 million, $7.6 million, and $7.8 million, respectively, in 2023, $0.4 million, $7.6 million, and $7.8 million, respectively, in 2024, and for Units 3 and 4 of $7.6 million and $7.8 million, respectively, in 2025. Effective August 1, 2023, the Company is amortizing $7.6 million annually until the next base rate case, as ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 43838, for the funding of future costs related to decommissioning Plant Vogtle Unit 3. As ordered by the Georgia PSC in Docket No. 29849, and as a result of Plant Vogtle Unit 4 being placed in service on April 29, 2024, the Company is amortizing $7.8 million annually effective May 1, 2024 until the next base rate case, for the funding of future costs related to decommissioning Plant Vogtle Unit 4. The recovery of the funding for Plant Vogtle Unit 1 will be determined by the Georgia PSC in the next base rate case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-38" id="fn-38" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In accordance with the Georgia PSC order in Docket No. 44280, costs associated with investigation and implementation of providing hourly usage information to all metered customers is to be recovered over a three-year period ending December 31, 2025. In the third quarter 2024, recovery of these costs in a regulatory asset, FERC 182.3, exceeded total expenditures of the program and the excess recovered amount is classified as a regulatory liability and amortization will be determined by the Georgia PSC in future regulatory proceedings.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-39" id="fn-39" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In accordance with the Georgia PSC order in Docket No. 44280 any revenue erosion resulting from the conversion of additional customers to a specific time-of-use rate will be deferred and recovered from customers in 2023 through 2025 through the annual compliance filings. In the third quarter 2025, recovery of these costs in a regulatory asset, FERC 182.3, exceeded total expenditures of the program and the excess recovered amount is classified as a regulatory liability and amortization will be determined by the Georgia PSC in future regulatory proceedings.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-40" id="fn-40" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Pursuant to the Commission&#8217;s Order in Docket Nos. 44160 and 43895, the portion of revenues associated with PPA additional sum and transmission fees that are collected from customers from the Customer Renewable Supply Procurement program are classified as a regulatory liability and amortization will be determined by the Georgia PSC in future regulatory proceedings.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-41" id="fn-41" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In accordance with the Georgia PSC order in Docket No. 44280 approving the Income-Qualified Discount (IQD) program, amounts included for recovery in rates as compared to actual customer savings associated with the IQD program are classified as a regulatory liability and amortization will be determined by the Georgia PSC in future regulatory proceedings.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-42" id="fn-42" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In accordance with the 2022 ARP Extension Stipulation in Docket No. 44280, certain regulatory assets, which were fully amortized as of December 31, 2025, will continue to be amortized over the 2022 ARP extension period, resulting in a regulatory liability. Future recovery will be determined in the next base rate base.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-43" id="fn-43" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
